# Cloudflare Pages custom headers.
#
# JS/CSS get a short-lived cache with forced revalidation -- Pages' default
# (Cache-Control: max-age=14400) meant the CDN edge would happily keep
# serving an old cached pro-wallet.js/aadhaar-qr-scan.js/style.css for up
# to 4 hours after a deploy, even though the new version was already live
# at origin. Confirmed directly: cf-cache-status: HIT on the plain URL
# serving stale content, while a cache-busted request to the same URL got
# the new deploy immediately -- the deploy itself was never the problem,
# the edge cache was. `no-cache` still lets the CDN/browser cache the
# response, but forces a revalidation (conditional request against the
# ETag Pages already sets) before ever serving it, so a real code change
# shows up on the next request instead of silently waiting out the cache.
#
# NOTE: Cloudflare Pages' _headers wildcard matches whole path segments,
# not an extension glob -- an earlier version of this file used `/*.js`
# and `/*.css`, which silently matched nothing (confirmed live: a
# cache-busted, guaranteed-fresh request still came back with the old
# default Cache-Control). Every JS/CSS file is listed explicitly instead.
/aadhaar-qr-scan.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/aadhaar-qr.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/field-mapping.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/forms-data.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/i18n.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/landing.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/pdf-generate.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/photo-editor.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/pro-wallet.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/pwa-install.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/task-pricing.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/ui.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/legal.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/style.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
